      "final_answer": "`STARTUP = timedelta(minutes=2)` at line 123 is a **session-to-launch matching window**, not a subagent/workflow routing timeout.\n\n- Matching uses session `created_at`: `launch.start < created_at <= min(launch.end, launch.start + STARTUP)` (line 461).\n- It requires the same working folder, exactly one candidate launch, and no competing session in that window. Explicit session-ID matches bypass the window.\n- A successful match restores recorded tool exclusions\u2014including agent/workflow tools. By default, new prompt/flag routing does not override those exclusions; `TOKENMASTER_RESUME_ESCALATE` enables additive unlocking.\n- If matching fails, routing runs afresh. Sessions created after two minutes\u2014or exactly at the launch timestamp\u2014cannot match through this fallback.\n\nThe two-minute value is consistent with the documented probe observations (startup within nine seconds), but remains a heuristic. Repository untouched.",
